{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016443-2e-making-chronicle-mystery-more-interesting","id":1016443,"title":"[2E] Making chronicle Mystery more interesting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-13T00:21:09-08:00","id":1016443,"title":"[2E] Making chronicle Mystery more interesting","content":"So 2E games should be centered on common Obsession of PCs, mostly main Mystery of particular chronicle. This topic is for helping with making it more incentive for players to dwell into. And here is my example of problem.<br /> <br /> I run Boston game with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/668690-mystery-supernal-alchemy-philosopher-s-stone?p=876709#post876709\">main Mystery as Philosophers Stone</a>. Players get their shards of Stone, some of the used, some of them don\u2019t \u2013 and they Awakened. They are now novice in Orders, about half of time in their studies. PCs seems to forgotten about Stones and I want them to remember them it. I asking what could make them more interested in topic?<br /> <br /> Lately, they are joined by Promethean Tammuz that wants to find answers on his own questions. Of course, for crossover purpose, his generated Vitroil <i>is </i>Philosophers Stone. Still, it can take a while before PCs will guide him to Milestones to understand his role in all this.<br /> <br /> I need something to make PCs more interested in the dwelling into Stone's Mystery. I thought about adding jealous Alchemist that want to steal it from PCs, but this seems a bit extreme, don\u2019t you think? Or maybe I should strive to add antagonist on PCs Obsession to the story? Any ideas or hints are more than welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-13-2016, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T00:41:52-08:00","id":1016449,"title":"","content":"Well, what <i>are </i>your group's players interested in, then? Why and how did the cabal first gather and form? The Philosopher's Stone, right? While individual mages are free to pursue personal advancement both social and mystic, as a team they should also have an eye on what brought them together.<br /> <br /> You could just say the sheer mystical weight of the Philosopher's Stone is causing the Nimbus of mages who contacted it the most intimately to gravitate towards it. The cabal finds that every Obsession that pings on their individual radars is tangentially related to the Stone, so they decide to gather up once more and chase this meta-mystery that almost seems to call them towards it.<br /> <br /> For mechanical incentives... a Promethean and an Alchemist should be a bounty of Arcane Beats themselves, wouldn't they? It might also clue them into this &quot;Divine Fire&quot; that no other mage seems to have dominion over...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T01:38:25-08:00","id":1016457,"title":"","content":"To make a central Mystery something that your players are interested in it should have an impact on their personal interests instead of expecting them to be interested in it just because it's the central Mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T08:29:41-08:00","id":1016569,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#737F8D\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In my experience, simply having something being unknown isn't often enough to drive *player* interest. Sure, I can set something in front of them that matches up with their character's obsessions, and the players will be all &quot;Obviously I'm doing that, my character is obsessed with that.&quot; But that's not when they're white-hot *needing* to find out what happens next, that's them simulating their characters as opposed to passionately diving headlong into the game.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#737F8D\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The answer, I've found, is to maintain a Dramatic Question, and an unresolved conflict. IT also helps if you can tie current goals and obstacles to past experiences in the story, somehow.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#737F8D\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Can the PC's use the [plot device] to accomplish the [thing that must be done] before the [consequences for failure]?&quot; is the formula I've used as of late, hasn't let me down yet. Mage requires a leetle beet of finagling to make it work; as the characters are virtually all-powerful and nothing is ever *really* beyond their grasp to tangibly accomplish -- so I really lay a heavy focus on the consequences of decisions the PC's make.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#737F8D\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I complicate things by making their obstacles the kinds of things that while easily ignored, overpowered or resolved, would have heavy consequences for simply taking the easy path through. I always stay focused on the long-term impacts of actions the PC's take; positive or negative. Rivals wait to pounce on the PC's mistakes, allies' political strength build off their successes. Banishers and Guardians make life difficult for mages who use obvious magic in sleepers' presence. Obligations from pacts the mages have struck in previous adventures could become problematic for immediate-solution thinking.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#737F8D\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">------------</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#737F8D\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As an example, in a recent story the PC's were doing a favor for a Councilor. In previous games, the PC's had encountered a Mage who was using some freaky martial arts to taint sleeper's organs. SLeepers would go mad and eventually die; if their organs were transplanted into another human, that human would become this massively dangerous rampaging abyssal monster. I got the whole plot of it from Intrusions - Encounters with the Abyss.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#737F8D\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But I'd added a single twist: Rarely, one of the people who underwent this abyssal process would, rather than going mad, Awaken. Their soul would shed the Curse by force. Sleepers had two reactions: give in, or be free.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#737F8D\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Catalyst was a mage who shared a mutual mentor with one of our PC's -- the three of them were Blank Badges. Catalyst realized he'd found a method to attempt actual Awakenings, so when the PC's confronted him, he vanished. Went hardcore underground. Was never heard from for a few stories.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#737F8D\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Then this story comes up: A seemingly unrelated investigation crosses paths with Catalyst. After a while, with the new information they'd discovered, Catalysts' whereabouts were much easier to divine. They could just roll up on him and finally take him in... except.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#737F8D\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">He'd holed up inside of a rival cabal's territory. A rival cabal that had dragged the Party through political hell in the first adventure of the game, and had served as the party's primary political antagonists ever since. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#737F8D\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sure, the party COULD just roll up on Catalysts' secret hideout in their Rival's territory -- and they even have sufficient magic to probably get away with it. For now. They're probably 3rd and 4th degree masters at this point.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#737F8D\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But if they did, and they slipped up even a *little bit*? It's gonna be a loooong, loooong road of political and legal consequences, a shitload of spotlight from the conciliar court, and a lot of ammunition in their rival's guns to make their lives miserable. And even if they ARE working for a councilor at the moment, they're only really doing that because if they don't, the run the risk of the council discovering their other less-than-acceptable practices, investigations and other work.</span></span><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Edit: Got really carried away on the consequences note; that wasn't the point. A focus on consequences was just necessary to fuel actual tension/drama into a game based on task-oriented dramatic questions without constantly relying on 'equal and opposite' antagonists for every story, by my experience.<br /> <br /> <b>TLDR</b>: Read up on Dramatic Questions, and provide your players conflicts. Mix the Central Mystery into those things; make one depend upon the other. That's what gets my table fired up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":12721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","user":"EvilSqueegee","date":". 12-13-2016, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T08:54:27-08:00","id":1016581,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12721_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12721\" data-vbnamecard=\"12721\">EvilSqueegee</a>, I'm running now apprentices game, not 'multiple masters' ( that's the other one I ST ). In lower-powered one PCs are only two weeks after Awakening and they still craving their place in Pentacle society. Once you are Adept, plots write themselves, but I want to make engaging playing in lower strata of power-level, at least for few more sessions. But I will read more on Dramatic Question.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016443-2e-making-chronicle-mystery-more-interesting?p=1016457#post1016457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To make a central Mystery something that your players are interested in it should have an impact on their personal interests instead of expecting them to be interested in it just because it's the central Mystery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts of the people they sacrificed for getting Philosophers Stones should work okay then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T09:15:12-08:00","id":1016590,"title":"","content":"Edit: re-read @Wyrdhamster's reply. Totally misunderstood it. I'm a dolt, it has been corrected. Carry on!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":12721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","user":"EvilSqueegee","date":". 12-13-2016, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T11:06:41-08:00","id":1016650,"title":"","content":"The ghosts would work well for the 'stick' but don't forget the 'carrot'. Give them a clues for ways the stones can still help them, something they (or others) would want to exploit. If I remember correctly you said that Nicholas Flamel is still around and he was the one who initiated all of this to begin with, he must have had a reason? Have him do something to kick them in their complacent shorts. If nothing else the reminder that there is a really old and powerful Mage lurking in the background, manipulating them, should get them riled up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T11:23:58-08:00","id":1016658,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12721_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12721\" data-vbnamecard=\"12721\">EvilSqueegee</a>, read on Dramatic Questions - Can't it simply be<br /> 'Will PCs uncover secret of Philosophers Stone?'<br /> <br /> I'm a bit tired of 'we must save world' plots to run, wanted to run something like real mystery ( and Mystery ) in <b>Mage</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016443-2e-making-chronicle-mystery-more-interesting?p=1016650#post1016650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ghosts would work well for the 'stick' but don't forget the 'carrot'. Give them a clues for ways the stones can still help them, something they (or others) would want to exploit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stone can help them by creating (almost) any spell effect they want. It simply is very useful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016443-2e-making-chronicle-mystery-more-interesting?p=1016650#post1016650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember correctly you said that Nicholas Flamel is still around and he was the one who initiated all of this to begin with, he must have had a reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>He wanted to see what they will do with his power. Also, wanting them to create the Stone themselves ( Archmastery? ) and by this making him 'Father of Alchemy'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016443-2e-making-chronicle-mystery-more-interesting?p=1016650#post1016650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have him do something to kick them in their complacent shorts.</div> </div> </div> </div>But why? He wanted to see what they will do with his 'gift' - maybe becoming his students on their own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016443-2e-making-chronicle-mystery-more-interesting?p=1016650#post1016650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If nothing else the reminder that there is a really old and powerful Mage lurking in the background, manipulating them, should get them riled up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Archmage. But still, it's more 'you can do what you want with my gift, I just watch for you from afar' kinda thing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-13-2016, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T14:44:42-08:00","id":1016748,"title":"","content":"If it was me being watched by an archmage, I'd want to know what the heck I could do to get me off his radar! If that meant studying what he had given me, I'd do it. If that meant giving/throwing away his &quot;gift,&quot; I'd do that too! <br /> I guess what I'm saying is, if your group doesn't know that old Nicholas is an archmage, just knowing might give them the kick you want. If they do know, then they ought to be reminded of just how powerful and dangerous an archmage is. In either case I would have your group overhear someone from the concilium talking about the &quot;incident.&quot; These other mages would probably whisper in conspiratorial tones, and would be scared themselves.<br /> <br /> So that's the stick side of things. As to the carrot side, perhaps the group isn't the only ones with pieces of a stone. Someone else is rising to power quickly, but they've been found out to be using a philosopher's stone. It's been confiscated by the Mysterium, and the mage is looking to replace it. He's willing to barter with your players' pcs to get his hands on another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","user":"Falcon777","date":". 12-13-2016, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T15:28:10-08:00","id":1016772,"title":"","content":"If the central mystery is &quot;what will you do with the power of the stones?&quot; then the answer is what they are currently doing with them, even if that answer is not a hell of a lot. If you want to bring the stones back front and center then you are going to need a new mystery, preferably one that either focuses on the stones or can only be unraveled using the stones.<br /> \u200bPerhaps the presence of so many stones in one place has an unexpected effect that even Flamel wasn't expecting. Maybe it thins or thickens the local gauntlet, or causes doors to the Underworld to open. Perhaps it creates bubbles of anti mana like in Tokyo, or the opposite effect like the Combat Zone of Boston.<br /> \u200bThey could cause one of the Bound to stir, or flickers of a 'Time Before'. If your chronicle is in London then where might the walking runes lead someone carrying a stone?<br /> \u200bWhat I'm trying to suggest is that maybe the mystery of the stones leads to another, unpredicted mystery, a new direction for your chronicle.<br /> You've hinted that the stones might serve as a mile stone on one Promethean's pilgrimage, what about the others? What happens if London starts drawing Prometheans like flies, and can the stones be used to limit the damage such a gathering will cause?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T17:46:56-08:00","id":1016836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1016443-2e-making-chronicle-mystery-more-interesting?p=1016658#post1016658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12721_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12721\" data-vbnamecard=\"12721\">EvilSqueegee</a>, read on Dramatic Questions - Can't it simply be<br /> 'Will PCs uncover secret of Philosophers Stone?'.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the first part of a dramatic question, you need the second part, the 'or else' it doesn't have to be world shattering. Will the PCs uncover the secret of the Philosopher's Stone in time to stop that asshole from becoming immortal? Will the PCs uncover the secret of the Philosopher's Stone before it gets stolen by that other asshole who wants it? Will the PCs uncover the secret of the Philosopher's Stone in time to use it to keep the Tower of Geburah from crumbling into ruins? Etc. What makes a Dramatic Question dramatic is that there's a meaningful consequence hanging in the balance. It doesn't have to be about the world ending. If the question is just, &quot;Will PCs uncover the secret of the Philosopher's Stone?&quot; and you stop there then there's no reason for anyone to care. Figure out the other half of the question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T19:35:13-08:00","id":1016873,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys, I now have much stronger grasp of what I want to do with Main Mystery. I will probably go with question 'Can they uncover secrets of Philosophers Stone... or else it destroys them?' - in my mind, unused Stones works as 'non-person' Soul Stones. They nihil Paradox and let magic work. You cannot summon dead or use sympathy to someone else, like with classical Soul Stone, as Philosophical Stones are much less than true Soul Stone. Still, true power of Philosophical ones is in the 'One Miracle' you can 'transmute' with it - any possible spell to Arcana's 5th dot is possible with them. Only change must be made directly on the target ( so no Spirit magic as it's outsiders forces reacting on target ).<br /> <br /> The problem with Philosophers Stones is that they are also Azoth condensed, just like Prometheans, but on smaller scale. And just like Created, Philosophers Stone create Wasteland effect, slowly but surely build-up around them. You just cannot let Stones to lay in your magical vault, or Firestorm will come one you. You <i>must</i> use them. Or it end like Boston's Combat Zone. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> On mechanics, I think about Stones using last touched creatures Supernatural Advantage as their Azoth rating - some freshly Awakened novices? Okay, it's only Azoth 1. But let your Consiliors of Gnosis 5-6 touch it, and we start to have problems. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It also means that Philosophers Stone awakens dormant Pandorans and glow for the hungry of Pyros Alchemists, calling them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Beside connecting Boston's Combat Zone as possible effects of unused Stone, I think about letting the high number of them in one place for longer time could lead into summoning of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/784966-2ed-boston-new-england-setting?p=827351#post827351\">Spirit of The Land</a>, that is connected to Secret Concord.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7825\" data-vbnamecard=\"7825\">Falcon777</a>, <i>how</i> lesser mages can know they are watched by Archmages? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> When you have only like Prime 3 you are totally safe from uncovering of your peeping time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T03:10:03-08:00","id":1016967,"title":"","content":"Can you perhaps show a rival Mage/Cabal that also have the Stones raising to power unexpectedly. If they poke a little they find out the Stones are the source of their success. Maybe then they will be more interested in active use of the Stones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}